        <h2 class="section">Recitals (WHEREAS)</h2>

        <p>WHEREAS the father of the Vendor is son of late Satyanarayana Singh having share in the land in
        Sy.No.127, 129, 130, 133, 134, 145, 147, 148 &amp; 149 total admeasuring Ac.21: 19 guntas, situated
        at Puppalguda Village, Rajendra Nagar Mandal, presently in Gandipet Mandal, Ranga Reddy District,
        Telangana State.</p>

        <p>WHEREAS the brother of late Satyanarayana Singh namely Dhan Singh during his life time filed a suit
        for partition and separate possession in respect of land in Sy.127, 129, 130, 133, 134, 145, 147, 148
        &amp; 149 admeasuring Ac.21 : 19 guntas, situated at Puppalguda Village, presently in Gandipet Mandal,
        Ranga Reddy District, vide O.S.No.473 of 2000 on the file of Hon'ble IV Additional Senior Civil Judge
        (FTC), Ranga Reddy District at L.B. Nagar against the Satyanarayana Singh and Ramesh Singh and after
        contest the said suit was dismissed in the year 2009. Aggrieved by the said Judgment Dhan Singh
        preferred appeal before the Hon&#8217;ble High Court of Telangana vide A.S.No.552 of 2009.</p>

        <p>During pending of the appeal Dhan Singh, Satyanarayana Singh and Ramesh Singh were died and their
        legal heirs have brought on record and thereafter due to the intervention of the family elders and
        well-wishers the matter has been settled between the parties amicably and accordingly all the parties
        entered into a memorandum of compromise dated 14-08-2020 and the same has been filed in A.S.No.552 of
        2009 before the Hon&#8217;ble High Court of Telangana and after recording the compromise the
        Hon&#8217;ble High Court pleased to disposed the appeal in terms of the compromise vide orders dated
        23-09-2020.</p>

        <p>WHEREAS late Satyanarayana Singh during the pending of the partition suit vide O.S.No.473 of 2000
