        <h2 class="section">5. Time is Essence</h2>
        <p>The DEVELOPER shall abide by the time schedule for completing the project as disclosed at the time
        of registration, subject to the VENDEE/S making payments as per schedule.</p>

        <h2 class="section">6. Construction of the Flat</h2>
        <p>The VENDEE/S have seen and accepted the sanction plan, specifications, amenities, floor plan and
        payment plan approved by the competent authority. The DEVELOPER shall develop the Project in
        accordance with the said sanction plan.</p>

        <h2 class="section">7. Possession of the Flat</h2>
        <p>7.1 The DEVELOPER assures to hand over possession of the Schedule B property by
        <span class="bold">June-2028</span> with a grace period of 6 months, subject to Force Majeure. On
        Force Majeure making the contract impossible, the agreement stands terminated and the DEVELOPER shall
        refund the entire amount received within 90 days.</p>
        <p>7.2 Procedure for taking possession &#8212; on/after obtaining the Occupancy Certificate, the
        Developer shall offer possession in writing; the Vendee shall take possession within two months.</p>
        <p>7.3 / 7.4 Failure to take possession; handover of documents &amp; common areas to the Association
        within thirty days after completion certificate. House-warming subject to clearance of all dues and
        NOC from Developer.</p>
        <p>7.5 Cancellation by VENDEE/S &#8212; where the Vendee cancels without fault of the Developer, the
        Developer may deduct 10% of Total Sale Consideration; balance returned within three months or on
        resale, whichever is later.</p>
        <p>7.6 Transfer rights &#8212; not allowed to sell/transfer till Two years from the date of Agreement
        or project completion (whichever later); one-time nomination of a blood relative permitted; resale not
        below prevailing base price and Rs.150/- per SFT to be paid with NOC.</p>
        <p>7.7 If the Developer fails to deliver possession by the date in Clause 7.1, it shall compensate at
        Rs.5/- per sq. ft of super built-up area per month of delay.</p>

        <h2 class="section">8. Representations and Warranties of the Developer</h2>
        <p>8.1 The DEVELOPER represents and warrants: (i) absolute, clear and marketable title; (ii) lawful
        rights and requisite approvals; (iii) Project Finance obtained from &#8220;CAPRI GLOBAL CAPITAL
        LIMITED&#8221;; (iv) no pending litigation except disclosed in title report; (v) valid approvals,
        licenses and permits; (vi)-(viii) right to enter into this Agreement, no conflicting agreements, not
        restricted from selling; (ix) handover of vacant peaceful possession at sale deed; (x)-(xi) discharge
        of governmental dues and no acquisition notice.</p>
        <p>The VENDEE/S covenants to maintain the Flat in good repair; not store hazardous goods; not
        demolish/alter structure; not alter elevation/colour scheme; not throw refuse; pay security deposits
        and local taxes; observe Society rules and pay taxes/outgoings punctually; permit the Promoter to
        inspect; and pay applicable Property Tax from registration date.</p>

        <h2 class="section">9. Events of Defaults and Consequences</h2>
        <p>9.1 The DEVELOPER is in default if it fails to provide ready-to-move-in possession within Para 7.1
        time or discontinues business due to suspension/revocation of registration.</p>
        <p>9.2 On Developer default, the VENDEE/S may stop further payments until milestones are corrected, or
        terminate and obtain full refund with interest within ninety days; if not withdrawing, receive
        interest for each month of delay.</p>
        <p>9.3 The VENDEE/S is in default on failure to pay 1 consecutive demand; continued default beyond 1
        month after notice allows cancellation and refund after deducting booking amount and interest, with
        30 days&#8217; prior intimation; repayment within ninety days or on resale, whichever later.</p>

        <h2 class="section">10. Conveyance of the Said Flat</h2>
        <p>The DEVELOPER, on receipt of the total price, shall execute a conveyance/sale deed and convey title
        with proportionate undivided share within 3 months from issuance of occupancy/completion certificate.
        Stamp duty and registration charges to be paid by the VENDEE/S.</p>

        <h2 class="section">11. Maintenance of the Said Building / Flat</h2>
        <p>11.1&#8211;11.9 The DEVELOPER provides essential services till takeover by the Association; may
        appoint a Property Management Company (PMC). Club house and common service connections maintained by
        the Developer; AMCs and insurance for lifts, STP, etc. form part of maintenance charges. User charges
        apply for Club House, Gym, Swimming Pool. The DEVELOPER reserves the right to maintain common areas
        for initial two years from commencement of pre-paid maintenance; VENDEE/S to pay Rs.4/- per sft for
        2 years as maintenance and corpus charges (club house excluded), payable normally 1 month before
        handover.</p>

        <h2 class="section">12. Defect Liability</h2>
        <p>12.1 Structural/workmanship defects notified within 5 years from handover shall be rectified
        without charge within 30 days, failing which the VENDEE/S receives compensation under the Act.</p>
        <p>12.2 Exclusions: equipment with manufacturer guarantees (lifts, generator, motors, STP,
        transformers, gym equipment, windows); plumbing/sanitary/electrical fittings with natural wear and
        tear; allowable structural deformations; painting and similar wear-and-tear works.</p>
        <p>12.3 The VENDEE/S / Association shall maintain flats and services in good condition with AMC and
        insurance.</p>

        <h2 class="section">13. Right to Enter the Flat for Repairs</h2>
        <p>The DEVELOPER / maintenance agency / Association shall have unrestricted access to common areas,
        garages and parking for maintenance, and may enter the Schedule B property after due notice during
        normal working hours.</p>

        <h2 class="section">14. Usage</h2>
        <p>Basements and service areas are earmarked for parking and services (electric sub-station,
        transformer, DG set rooms, water tanks, pump rooms, firefighting, etc.) and shall not be used by the
        VENDEE/S for any other purpose.</p>

        <h2 class="section">15. General Compliance with Respect to the Flat</h2>
        <p>15.1&#8211;15.15 The VENDEE/S shall maintain the Schedule B property at own cost; not put signage,
        neon lights or advertisements on the building exterior; not change exterior colour/elevation; plan
        electrical load per installed systems; pay user charges for Clubhouse/Gym/Swimming pool; no structural
        modifications (Shear Wall Technology); not demolish or enclose balconies/parking with grills; keep
        drains and pipes in good condition; share common over-head tank and pay water charges by meter; fix
        AC units only at designated locations; dry clothes only in Utility areas; keep common areas clear;
        not modify sit-outs/corridors/main door; name boards per Developer design; use the Flat for
        residential purposes only. The exclusive Verandah &#8220;Sit-Out&#8221; area shall not be
        covered/barricaded except on payment of not less than Rs.20,00,000/- to the Association into the
        Corpus Account. Planter boxes and windows fixed per architectural elevation; plants as defined by the
        DEVELOPER.</p>

        <h2 class="section">16. Compliance of Laws, Notifications etc. by Parties</h2>
        <p>The Parties enter into this Agreement with full knowledge of all laws, rules, regulations and
        notifications applicable to the project.</p>

        <h2 class="section">17. Additional Constructions</h2>
        <p>The DEVELOPER undertakes not to make additions or additional structures after the approved plans,
        except as provided in the Act and as set out in this Agreement.</p>

        <h2 class="section">18. Mortgage or Create a Charge</h2>
        <p>The VENDEE/S authorizes the DEVELOPER to raise finance by charge/mortgage of the Flat/Project,
        provided the Flat shall be free from encumbrances at the time of Sale Deed execution.</p>

        <h2 class="section">19. Miscellaneous</h2>
        <p>19.1 Tri-partite Agreement where the VENDEE/S avails a housing loan; the VENDEE/S obligation to pay
        the total sale consideration is independent of the bank loan.</p>
        <p>19.2 The building is named &#8220;THE LEGACEY&#8221;; the DEVELOPER may erect display/name boards
        permanently.</p>
        <p>19.3 The Vendee acknowledges the Developer has applied for two additional floors (23rd and 24th)
        using TDR; such floors are the exclusive property of the Developer and the Vendee shall have no right
        or claim therein and shall sign required documents without objection.</p>
        <p>19.4 Interior works allowed only after handover; permitted between 8:00 AM and 7:00 PM; penalty for
        interiors beyond 4 months of handover.</p>
        <p>19.5 The purchaser agrees to pay Rs.96/- per Sq. Ft. plus 18% GST as 2-year maintenance; one-time
        Move-in charges Rs.25,000/- plus 18% GST; fixed electricity for 3 months; interim maintenance Rs.2/-
        per Sq. Ft. plus 18% GST per month; and Rs.25,000/- plus 18% GST towards legal and documentation
        charges at Sale Deed registration. Bore-well deepening expenses to be shared proportionately by all
        Flat Owners.</p>
        <p>19.6 Parking places allotted by lottery method. 19.7 CCTV only for drive-ways, entry &amp; exit
        ramps (no individual parking slots). 19.8 Vehicles to be parked only in allotted parking lots.</p>

        <h2 class="section">20. Formation of Association of VENDEE/S</h2>
        <p>The DEVELOPER shall apply to the Registrar for registration of the Association as a society under
        the Telangana Societies Registration Act, 2001, within two months from issue of the occupation
        certificate where at least sixty per cent of VENDEE/S have taken possession and paid full
        consideration. After conveying title, the DEVELOPER may continue to market and sell unsold units.</p>

        <h2 class="section">21&#8211;34. General Provisions</h2>
        <p><span class="bold">21. Entire Agreement</span> &#8212; this Agreement with its schedules
        constitutes the entire agreement and supersedes all prior understandings.</p>
        <p><span class="bold">22. Right to Amend</span> &#8212; only through written consent of both Parties.</p>
        <p><span class="bold">23. Provisions Applicable on Subsequent VENDEE/S</span> &#8212; all provisions
        bind any subsequent VENDEE/S.</p>
        <p><span class="bold">24. Waiver Not a Limitation to Enforce</span> &#8212; waiver in one case is not
        a precedent; failure to enforce is not a waiver.</p>
        <p><span class="bold">25. Severability</span> &#8212; void/unenforceable provisions are deemed amended
        or deleted, remaining provisions stay valid.</p>
        <p><span class="bold">26. Method of Calculation of Proportionate Share</span> &#8212; in proportion to
        built-up, balcony, verandah, common and parking areas to the total built-up area.</p>
        <p><span class="bold">27. Further Assurances</span> &#8212; parties shall execute additional
        instruments as reasonably required.</p>
        <p><span class="bold">28. Place of Execution</span> &#8212; deemed executed at Hyderabad; registered
        at the office of the Sub-Registrar, Gandipet, Ranga Reddy.</p>
